192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 90 0 R
/T (The trigger was an energy shock meeting resilient growth. ICE Brent traded near US$105 a barrel, up US$21 since early August, while the US flash composite PMI rose to 58.4. That combination left central banks with little room to ease: the Fed raised its target range to 3.75% to 4.00%, and the ECB lifted its deposit rate to 2.50%. Supply is heavy at the same time. The US Treasury expects US$628bn of privately held net borrowing in Q4, US corporate issuance reached US$2.20tn through September \(+24.5% year on year\), and the AI buildout adds a new financing programme. Central banks are not taking up the slack. The ECB is running down its APP and PEPP holdings, and the Fed now only rolls over maturing Treasury principal and reinvests agency principal in Treasury bills, so it is not adding long-duration demand.)
/E (The trigger was an energy shock meeting resilient growth. ICE Brent traded near US$105 a barrel, up US$21 since early August, while the US flash composite PMI rose to 58.4. That combination left central banks with little room to ease: the Fed raised its target range to 3.75% to 4.00%, and the ECB lifted its deposit rate to 2.50%. Supply is heavy at the same time. The US Treasury expects US$628bn of privately held net borrowing in Q4, US corporate issuance reached US$2.20tn through September \(+24.5% year on year\), and the AI buildout adds a new financing programme. Central banks are not taking up the slack. The ECB is running down its APP and PEPP holdings, and the Fed now only rolls over maturing Treasury principal and reinvests agency principal in Treasury bills, so it is not adding long-duration demand.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
