249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 92 0 R
/T (Central banks set the overnight rate, but investors price the years that follow. A 10y yield reflects the expected average path of short-term rates over the next decade, plus extra compensation for holding duration. That compensation covers the risk that inflation runs hotter than expected, that heavy government borrowing pushes yields higher, and that an investor may need to sell before maturity in a weaker market. When any of those risks rises, long yields can climb even if the central bank does nothing.)
/E (Central banks set the overnight rate, but investors price the years that follow. A 10y yield reflects the expected average path of short-term rates over the next decade, plus extra compensation for holding duration. That compensation covers the risk that inflation runs hotter than expected, that heavy government borrowing pushes yields higher, and that an investor may need to sell before maturity in a weaker market. When any of those risks rises, long yields can climb even if the central bank does nothing.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 92 0 R
/T (The US move reached the whole curve \(Exhibit 1\). Between 1 September and 6 October, the 2y yield rose 40bps, the 5y and 7y rose 48bps to 49bps, the 10y rose 48bps and the 30y rose 37bps. Because the front and middle of the curve moved as much as the long end, this was not simply investors abandoning the longest maturities. Markets can become less sure about the next policy meeting while still expecting money to stay expensive for longer, and it is that longer view that drives the price of a 5y or 10y bond.)
/E (The US move reached the whole curve \(Exhibit 1\). Between 1 September and 6 October, the 2y yield rose 40bps, the 5y and 7y rose 48bps to 49bps, the 10y rose 48bps and the 30y rose 37bps. Because the front and middle of the curve moved as much as the long end, this was not simply investors abandoning the longest maturities. Markets can become less sure about the next policy meeting while still expecting money to stay expensive for longer, and it is that longer view that drives the price of a 5y or 10y bond.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 92 0 R
/T (These charts cannot isolate the term premium on their own, because the move mixes changing rate expectations with changing compensation for risk. What they do show is that the repricing was broad and persistent. Even after partial rallies, benchmark yields stayed well above their earlier levels across the US, UK, France, Germany and Japan. That is now the starting point at which governments and companies have to finance heavy borrowing, before any credit spread is added on top.)
/E (These charts cannot isolate the term premium on their own, because the move mixes changing rate expectations with changing compensation for risk. What they do show is that the repricing was broad and persistent. Even after partial rallies, benchmark yields stayed well above their earlier levels across the US, UK, France, Germany and Japan. That is now the starting point at which governments and companies have to finance heavy borrowing, before any credit spread is added on top.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [17]
>>
