/E (Companies are adding to that supply. US corporate issuance reached US$2.20tn through September, 24.5% above the same period of 2025, spanning refinancing, M&A funding and new investment. AI is a fast-growing part of that demand for capital. S&P Global puts 2026 hyperscaler AI capex above US$700bn, against about US$80bn in 2019, and J.P. Morgan Asset Management expects US$279bn of bond issuance this year from the five hyperscalers alone. Not every dollar of AI spending becomes bond supply, since these companies also fund through operating cash flow, equity, bank loans and private credit. But the part that does reach the bond market competes for the same pool of investors, and the same appetite for duration, as government debt.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [35]
>>
endobj
