367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 95 0 R
/T (An IG index yield and a single 10y Treasury are not maturity-matched. The IG effective yield rose 46bps \(5.53% to 5.99%\) while the 10y Treasury rose 48bps; that co-movement is illustrative, not a precise attribution. The separately measured IG OAS widened only 2bps, consistent with limited credit spread repricing. A strong issuer can therefore face a higher coupon even with a stable spread. Lower down, rates and credit are compounding: HY effective yields reached 8.03% and CCC 16.98% by 6 October. Bank of America cut its October US IG issuance forecast from about US$160bn to US$110bn \(Financial Times\).)
/E (An IG index yield and a single 10y Treasury are not maturity-matched. The IG effective yield rose 46bps \(5.53% to 5.99%\) while the 10y Treasury rose 48bps; that co-movement is illustrative, not a precise attribution. The separately measured IG OAS widened only 2bps, consistent with limited credit spread repricing. A strong issuer can therefore face a higher coupon even with a stable spread. Lower down, rates and credit are compounding: HY effective yields reached 8.03% and CCC 16.98% by 6 October. Bank of America cut its October US IG issuance forecast from about US$160bn to US$110bn \(Financial Times\).)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
