/Title (The US move reached the whole curve \(Exhibit 1\). Between 1 September and 6 October, the 2y yield rose 40bps, the 5y and 7y rose 48bps to 49bps, the 10y rose 48bps and the 30y rose 37bps. Because the front and middle of the curve moved as much as the long end, this was not simply investors abandoning the longest maturities. Markets can become less sure about the next policy meeting while still expecting money to stay expensive for longer, and it is that longer view that drives the price of a 5y or 10y bond.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2891 0 R
/Prev 2908 0 R
/Next 2909 0 R
>>
endobj
