/Title (An IG index yield and a single 10y Treasury are not maturity-matched. The IG effective yield rose 46bps \(5.53% to 5.99%\) while the 10y Treasury rose 48bps; that co-movement is illustrative, not a precise attribution. The separately measured IG OAS widened only 2bps, consistent with limited credit spread repricing. A strong issuer can therefore face a higher coupon even with a stable spread. Lower down, rates and credit are compounding: HY effective yields reached 8.03% and CCC 16.98% by 6 October. Bank of America cut its October US IG issuance forecast from about US$160bn to US$110bn \(Financial Times\).)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2914 0 R
/Next 2935 0 R
>>
endobj
